{
  "description": "Scoring vectors for capability_trial (EKP 3.1). Each case gives an expectation, the provider's structured output and its declared output schema (null when it declares none), and the answer the network gives, scored without a model, or the error code it refuses the expectation with before calling the provider (`refused`); `exact_checks` gives each check's score before rounding, to four places. Each check's score is shown rounded down to a step of 0.25; the trial's score is the weighted mean of the exact scores of the checks that could be scored, the network's own `schema` check (weight 1) among them, rounded down to a step of 0.05. A check that can't be scored is cannot_tell and left out of the mean; with every check of the consumer's cannot_tell there is no score (null) and the trial doesn't pass. With no checks given, the schema check alone is the score.",
